{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>stone of rolling</b> — for it must be rolled because of its great heaviness." "<b>and timber is set in the walls</b> — cedar wood, for it is strong and does not rot — they would place in the walls so that the building would be strong." "<b>with haste</b> — meaning, quickly."], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra explains the Aramaic phrase אבן גלל as a stone requiring rolling."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:41:59.087871800Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}